"""RabbitMQ inter-service transport: one shared topic exchange.

Every service in a ``transport_rabbitmq`` mesh publishes to and/or consumes from
one shared, durable topic exchange (``APP_TRANSPORT_EXCHANGE``). Routing keys are
free-form dotted strings, conventionally ``<target-or-domain>.<event>``. A
consumer binds its own durable queue (``<service_name>.inbox``) to the patterns
it cares about.

This is deliberately thinner than the ``messaging_rabbitmq`` overlay (which is a
service's own work queue): here the exchange is the mesh's shared event bus.
"""

